cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the relevant companion paper and this software release."
title: "barker-quotient: A 2-Primary Quotient Framework for Barker Obstructions"
abstract: >-
  Source code, paper, and verification suite for the 2-primary quotient
  framework for the Barker sequence non-existence problem. Exhaustively
  enumerates the 421 minimal covering configurations of hard primes at
  k <= 6 over the first 80 hard primes, in six primary structural strata
  (plus the overlapping A_blocked refinement flag); proves the
  cofactor-cycle theorem at the full-hub (A1) spine with its structural
  cutoff, of which S = {17881, 1801, 14537, 13417, 18121, 18521} is the
  unique A1 instance at size 6 (the census contains 61 configurations at
  k = 6 in total); establishes a discrimination-depth ladder over the
  strata; and evaluates the reciprocity-symmetric skeleton null exactly,
  giving R(3,3,3,3) = 1373/5300 and R(3,3,3,4) = 1123/4215 and thereby
  disproving the depth-flatness earlier Monte-Carlo estimates suggested. A
  companion theorem proves that, after row-gauge reduction, reciprocity and
  the conditions involving 2 are the only global realizability constraints,
  and identifies the skeleton product measure as the exact per-prefix and
  iterated arithmetic law. It does not prove a simultaneous-height frequency
  theorem or a new Barker obstruction.
  The v1.0 release (2026-05-16) carried an earlier framing built on the
  Hub Self-Defeat Theorem and a 13-configuration Type A/B classification;
  that reading is superseded by the census.
